OL,3,GNEWSA'Knowing how to react when someone
OL,4,Adies is hard - here's the most
OL,5,Aimportant thing to do'
OL,6,
OL,7,FKnowing what to say or how to support
OL,8,Fsomeone after a bereavement can be
OL,9,Fdifficult. Fear of saying the wrong
OL,10,Fthing or intruding at a sensitive time
OL,11,Fcan leave people worried about getting
OL,12,Fit wrong and avoiding reaching out
OL,13,Faltogether.
OL,15,FBut Dr Lesel Dawson, from the
OL,16,FUniversity of Bristol, said this is the
OL,17,Fworst thing people can do.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1792041990
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSA'Knowing how to react when someone
OL,4,Adies is hard - here's the most
OL,5,Aimportant thing to do'
OL,6,
OL,7,FSpeaking ahead of an annual Good Grief
OL,8,FFestival that Dawson is co-director of,
OL,9,Fshe said: "The most important thing
OL,10,Fwhen helping someone dealing with grief
OL,11,Fisn't what you say, but that you don't
OL,12,Fturn away.
OL,14,F"A simply acknowledgement like, 'I'm so
OL,15,Fsorry and I'm here' can mean a great
OL,16,Fdeal and it's vital to let the grieving
OL,17,Fperson lead- to follow their pace,
OL,18,Ftheir language and their need to talk
OL,19,Fabout the person who died."
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
